# Publish to main

When feature work on this repo is done (or the user asks to publish / ship / merge):

1. Merge into local `main` (fast-forward preferred; otherwise merge commit).
2. Push `main` to `origin` (`git push -u origin main` if needed).
3. Do **not** open a PR unless the user explicitly asks for one.
4. Do **not** leave work only on a feature branch after the user asked to publish.

Still follow git safety: no force-push to `main`, no `--no-verify`, no amending others' commits.
